## Key Concepts
- Idempotency and idempotency keys
- Exactly-once processing vs at-least-once semantics
- Retries, backoff, and fault injection
- Mocking external services (payments, inventory)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example test sketch (pseudo)
describe('POST /orders idempotency', () => {
  it('returns same order on replay with same key', async () => {
    const key = 'abc-123'
    const payload = {customerId: 'C1', items: [{sku: 'S1', qty: 2}], address: 'X'}
    const r1 = await post('/orders', payload, {Idempotency-Key: key})
    const r2 = await post('/orders', payload, {Idempotency-Key: key})
    expect(r1.orderId).toBe(r2.orderId)
  })
})
```

